{"content":[{"text":"I want to implement the new <Scalar/> component. drop back to the desktop and launch a new SGI 3D visualizer desktop app.\n\nit should look like this [Image #4]\n\nHere are the steps:\n\nThere should be three spaces - two for two different users and one for a shared remote. There are several steps. User one writes a commit that has a tree that lists two values pointing to blob IDs A and B. Then adds another commit with a tree with 4 values (two existing, two new) and two new blobs C and D are added to the blob storage part. Then a \"prune\" happens that writes a new commit with a new tree of only C and D, no new blobs added. Then pushes all of this to the server. Then User 2 runs \"setup\", which pulls the trees and commits but only blobs C and D because they're in the tip. then there is a read for the key that points to A and just A is pulled from the server. use ../git-meta commands for the commands run.\n\n[external unsupported block: image]","type":"input_text"}],"event_id":"01a09493-9fb3-7940-8858-80b0243ebd64:8","role":"user","session_id":"01a09493-9fb3-7940-8858-80b0243ebd64","source_line":8,"timestamp":"2026-09-12T07:44:57.804Z","type":"message"}
